  "explanation": "\n\nAfter accounting for the 0.10 % per‑trade cost, the strategy lost about 13 % over the period, which is worse than the –10.8 % loss from simply holding TLT and far below the S&P 500’s +66.9 % gain on the same days. The approach was only invested 19 % of the time, yielded a negative Sharpe ratio of –0.10 and endured a maximum drawdown of roughly 26 %, showing poor risk‑adjusted performance. With no robustness check presented, the negative result appears more likely due to chance than a genuine edge, leading to a **Weak** verdict.",
  "code": "import yfinance as yf\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nimport json\nimport sys\n\ndef download_with_retry(ticker, start, tries=3, pause=3):\n    for attempt in range(tries):\n        df = yf.download(ticker, start=start, auto_adjust=True, progress=False)\n        if df is not None and not df.empty:\n            close = df[\"Close\"].squeeze()\n            if isinstance(close, pd.DataFrame):\n                close = close.iloc[:, 0]\n            return close.rename(ticker)\n        if attempt < tries - 1:\n            time.sleep(pause)\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to download {ticker} after {tries} attempts\")\n\ndef main():\n    START = \"2015-01-01\"\n    TRAD_TICKER = \"TLT\"\n    SIG_TICKER = \"^TNX\"\n    BENCH_TICKER = \"SPY\"\n\n    # --- Download Data ---\n    try:\n        tlt_close = download_with_retry(TRAD_TICKER, START)\n        tnx_close = download_with_retry(SIG_TICKER, START)\n        spy_close = download_with_retry(BENCH_TICKER, START)\n    except RuntimeError as e:\n        print(f'RESULT {{\"unsupported\": \"{e}\"}}')\n        sys.exit(0)\n\n    # --- Align Calendars (Inner Join) ---\n    # Only keep dates where ALL three tickers have actual data (no forward-fill).\n    data = pd.concat([tlt_close, tnx_close, spy_close], axis=1, join=\"inner\")\n    \n    if len(data) == 0:\n        print('RESULT {\"unsupported\": \"No overlapping dates between TLT, ^TNX, and SPY\"}')\n        return\n\n    tlt_close = data[TRAD_TICKER]\n    tnx_close = data[SIG_TICKER]\n    spy_close = data[BENCH_TICKER]\n\n    # --- Signal Calculation ---\n    # ^TNX (CBOE 10Y Yield) is quoted in PERCENT (e.g. 4.50 for 4.50%).\n    # 1 bp = 0.01%. 8 bps = 0.08%. 4 bps = 0.04%.\n    ENTRY_THRESHOLD = -0.08   # Down >= 8 bps\n    EXIT_THRESHOLD = 0.04     # Up >= 4 bps from entry close\n    MAX_HOLD_DAYS = 6\n\n    tnx_change = tnx_close.diff()\n\n    # --- Build Holding Array (State Machine) ---\n    holding = pd.Series(0.0, index=tlt_close.index, dtype=float)\n    state = 0          # 0=flat, 1=long\n    entry_tnx = 0.0\n    hold_days = 0\n\n    for i in range(len(tlt_close)):\n        tnx_today = tnx_close.iloc[i]\n        tnx_chg_today = tnx_change.iloc[i]\n\n        if state == 0:\n            # Entry Signal: TNX down >= 8bps vs prior close\n            if not np.isnan(tnx_chg_today) and tnx_chg_today <= ENTRY_THRESHOLD:\n                state = 1\n                entry_tnx = tnx_today\n                hold_days = 1\n                holding.iloc[i] = 1.0\n        elif state == 1:\n            # Exit Conditions at current close\n            tnx_chg_from_entry = tnx_today - entry_tnx\n            exit_cond = (not np.isnan(tnx_chg_from_entry) and tnx_chg_from_entry >= EXIT_THRESHOLD) or (hold_days >= MAX_HOLD_DAYS)\n            \n            holding.iloc[i] = 1.0  # Invested through today's close\n            \n            if exit_cond:\n                state = 0\n                hold_days = 0\n            else:\n                hold_days += 1\n\n    # --- Positions & Returns ---\n    # Position = Holding shifted by 1 (Enter at T close, earn T+1 return)\n    position = holding.shift(1).fillna(0.0)\n    \n    tlt_ret = tlt_close.pct_change().fillna(0.0)\n    spy_ret = spy_close.pct_change().fillna(0.0)\n    \n    strat_ret = position * tlt_ret\n\n    # Trading Costs: 0.1% per entry (round trip)\n    entries = (position.diff() == 1.0).astype(float)\n    strat_ret -= entries * 0.001\n\n    # Equity Curves\n    equity = (1.0 + strat_ret).cumprod()\n    bh_tlt_equity = (1.0 + tlt_ret).cumprod()\n    bh_spy_equity = (1.0 + spy_ret).cumprod()\n\n    # --- SPY Benchmarks (on Strategy Calendar) ---\n    # Spy Same Days Return: Compounded SPY return only on days strategy held position\n    spy_strat_ret = spy_ret * position\n    spy_same_days_equity = (1.0 + spy_strat_ret).cumprod()\n    spy_same_days_return = float(spy_same_days_equity.iloc[-1] - 1.0)\n\n    # Spy Random Days Return: Average SPY daily return compounded for n_days_in_position\n    n_days_in_pos = int(position.sum())\n    spy_mean_daily = spy_ret.mean()\n    spy_random_days_return = float((1.0 + spy_mean_daily) ** n_days_in_pos - 1.0)\n\n    # --- Metrics ---\n    total_return = float(equity.iloc[-1] - 1.0)\n    buy_and_hold_return = float(bh_tlt_equity.iloc[-1] - 1.0)\n    \n    # Sharpe (Annualized sqrt(252) for non-crypto)\n    if strat_ret.std() > 0:\n        sharpe = float((strat_ret.mean() / strat_ret.std()) * np.sqrt(252))\n    else:\n        sharpe = 0.0\n\n    # Max Drawdown\n    running_max = equity.cummax()\n    drawdown = equity / running_max - 1.0\n    max_drawdown = float(drawdown.min())\n\n    n_trades = int(entries.sum())\n    time_in_market = float(position.sum() / len(position))\n\n    # --- Save Equity CSV ---\n    eq_df = pd.DataFrame({\n        'date': equity.index,\n        'strategy': equity.values,\n        'spy': bh_spy_equity.values\n    })\n    eq_df.to_csv(\"equity.csv\", index=False)\n\n    # --- Print RESULT ---\n    result = {\n        \"traded_ticker\": TRAD_TICKER,\n        \"total_return\": total_return,\n        \"buy_and_hold_return\": buy_and_hold_return,\n        \"spy_same_days_return\": spy_same_days_return,\n        \"spy_random_days_return\": spy_random_days_return,\n        \"time_in_market\": time_in_market,\n        \"sharpe\": sharpe,\n        \"max_drawdown\": max_drawdown,\n        \"n_trades\": n_trades\n    }\n    print(f\"RESULT {json.dumps(result)}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
